       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Esmé Cowles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I don't believe there is any action required here — there are tests to verify that the Digest header behaves the same for GET and HEAD (\n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2598\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2598\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Ensure Digest header is the same for GET and HEAD\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2598\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n), so I think we can just close this.</p>",
     "created": "15/Sep/17 11:09 AM",
     "id": "19343",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12546/comment/19343",
